    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 46 tests pass. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date, returning HTTP 400.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Added `requireRegistrationDateNotInFuture(LocalDate)` helper that throws `InvalidFieldsException(List.of(\"registrationDate\"))` when a non-null supplied date is `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`. A `null` date is left alone since it's subsequently defaulted to the server date and can never be in the future.\n- Called it in `addOwner` on the raw supplied date (before defaulting and before business-day adjustment), so validation reflects exactly what the client sent.\n\nI reused the existing `InvalidFieldsException`, which the `ExceptionControllerAdvice` already maps to a 400 Bad Request with the offending field name in the `errors` array \u2014 consistent with how the other present-but-invalid field validations (email, postcode) are handled. No new exception class or advice handler was needed.\n\nThe new acceptance test `Cp33Tests.errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `2999-01-01`) passes, and the full suite remains green (46/46).",
